<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tiermes</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Termes, Termantia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tiermes, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> Termes, was a Celtiberian town of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arevaci">Arevaci</a> on a sandstone ridge in the modern province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soria">Soria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. It resisted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in the 2nd century BCE and later became a Roman municipium, with rock-cut houses, an aqueduct and a forum. The site was abandoned in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> and is now an archaeological park.</p></div>
